      "recommended_risk": "low",
      "technical_explanation": "The scanner flagged a regular expression it treats as potentially unsafe for catastrophic backtracking. The expressions visible in the supplied source near the flagged location are simple validators: a bounded language-code check that accepts only short alphabetic locale identifiers, a Font Awesome class-name check built from a single character class with one greedy quantifier, and trivial whitespace or newline matchers. None of these permit nested or overlapping quantifiers, so matching cost is linear in the input length. The values reaching them come from the extension's own locale manifest, which is additionally format-validated before use in a path, or from locally stored user button settings, which the project states are trimmed to a sane length. No denial-of-service path via these expressions is demonstrated. The evidence window is truncated, but every visible pattern-matching expression in the supplied source is safe.",
      "layman_explanation": "The scanning tool flagged a pattern-matching expression that can sometimes be slow under malicious input. The expressions in this file are simple checks on short pieces of text like language codes and icon names, so there is no realistic way to use them to freeze or crash the app.",
